    "word_count": 51,
    "html": "<p>Terri Wesselman is an American entrepreneur who co-founded Omniplex World Services with Julien Patterson and served as its chief executive. The company provided security and background investigations for government and commercial clients. After selling a majority stake to Altamont Capital Partners, she stepped back from executive leadership and developed other businesses.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "A converted petrol station became an art gallery when Terri Wesselman and her husband began creating businesses in Virginia's Northern Neck. Objects Art and More offered a gathering place as well as artwork. She also opened a homewares shop after noticing that local residents lacked somewhere to buy tableware for entertaining.\n\nAt their restaurant, The Office Bistro, she addressed another practical problem during a temporary closure for renovations. Employees could volunteer with a nonprofit organisation of their choice and receive pay for those hours. The arrangement was designed to maintain their income and keep their jobs available when the restaurant reopened.",
