    ],
    "word_count": 101,
    "html": "<p>A converted petrol station became an art gallery when Terri Wesselman and her husband began creating businesses in Virginia's Northern Neck. Objects Art and More offered a gathering place as well as artwork. She also opened a homewares shop after noticing that local residents lacked somewhere to buy tableware for entertaining.</p>\r\n<p>At their restaurant, The Office Bistro, she addressed another practical problem during a temporary closure for renovations. Employees could volunteer with a nonprofit organisation of their choice and receive pay for those hours. The arrangement was designed to maintain their income and keep their jobs available when the restaurant reopened.</p>\r\n"
  },
